+# Evidence for improving the skill
+
+Use a local case directory for each investigation. A useful record lets the
+next agent understand why an attempt failed without replaying the entire chat.
+
+## Capture an attempt
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/record_attempt.py --case CASE-ID --stage build \
+  --hypothesis 'The candidate module is the cause' \
+  --expected 'The module builds from the pinned source' \
+  --context-file case-context.json --timeout 600 -- COMMAND ARGUMENTS
+```
+
+The tool stores raw stdout/stderr, exit status, elapsed time, the command and
+selected locale variables. Non-UTF-8 output is retained byte for byte. Use
+`--expected-exit 1` for a reproducer that is supposed to demonstrate a bug.
+`--root DIRECTORY` selects another private record location; the default is
+`~/.local/share/fix-it-in-wine/cases`. Records are not uploaded automatically.
+
+The context JSON should contain the facts relevant to this attempt:
+
+- application version, executable path and architecture;
+- Wine command/version/tag, prefix architecture and whether it is disposable;
+- active DLLs, hashes, slots, overrides, source commit and patch hashes;
+- locale, DPI, screen dimensions, X11/Wayland and actual selected fonts;
+- baseline timings, cold/warm state and logging preset for performance work;
+- CI run, job and exact tested SHA when the experiment runs remotely.
+
+Do not guess missing values. State that they are unknown and collect only what
+the next decision needs. Keep unrelated environment variables and credentials
+out of the record. Exact arguments and raw output can still contain private
+paths or tokens; the directory is private and is not a publication artifact.
+
+## Record the outcome and recovery
+
+After each meaningful failure, add an observation next to its attempt record:
+
+1. Expected result and what actually happened. Include the exact error,
+   return code or signal; preserve the bytes and encoding for decoding errors.
+2. Which stage failed: download, checksum, source selection, patch application,
+   configure, compile, load, execution, visual behavior, timing or rollback.
+3. What was already changed. Record backup/state integrity, whether the DLL
+   and registry were restored, and the command that recovered the last good
+   state. Do not call an interrupted installation clean without checking.
+4. Evidence supporting or rejecting the hypothesis. Distinguish a product bug
+   from a test harness failure and “not reproduced” from “fixed.”
+5. The next experiment and why it adds information. Retain abandoned attempts
+   with a reason rather than quietly overwriting their evidence.
+
+For intermittent artifacts, record a timestamp, the preceding actions and the
+shortest bounded capture around the event. Preserve a screenshot and relevant
+log excerpt when available. A missing reproduction is not proof that the
+artifact is gone. Performance measurements should also run with verbose tracing
+disabled; a tracing slowdown is not a product benchmark.
+
+## Turn evidence into an improvement
+
+Propose one general correction supported by the failure and explain its
+limits. Add an observable regression check when appropriate. Examples from
+real workflow failures:
+
+- An OEM console message broke UTF-8 decoding after the DLL was replaced:
+  preserve raw bytes, decode with the right page, and query before mutation.
+- A pipeline ended in `tee` after Wine refused a prefix under a directory not
+  owned by the runner: use an owned work directory, `pipefail`, and verify the
+  expected program output/exit code before accepting green CI.
+- Destroying a test list-view also destroyed a shared image list: keep fixture
+  lifetimes explicit so later cases do not measure invalid resources.
+- An application key opened an exit confirmation instead of the desired view:
+  inspect the resulting window/screenshot before continuing the input sequence.
+
+Do not make an example into an unconditional rule for unrelated tasks. A
+proposed change still needs to be tried on the failing case. Follow the user's
+repository workflow: if they requested patches for another repository, deliver
+the patch instead of opening or merging a PR there.
+
+Raw logs, personal photos, full home paths and local account details stay in
+the private case directory. A public proposal uses synthetic fixtures and the
+smallest sanitized evidence that supports the change.
